-- Wires the Molten/Chromatic tier-token exchange (SS7.1/#13 of docs/coa/molten-core.md): Major
-- Mattingly (14394, Stormwind) and Overlord Runthak (14392, Orgrimmar) already exist with
-- "Classic Tier Sets" as their sub-name but an empty npc_vendor. The client's own
-- ItemExtendedCost.dbc (loaded verbatim by the core, src/server/game/DataStores/DBCStores.cpp,
-- no SQL override) already carries one row per Molten/Chromatic token id requiring exactly 1 of
-- that token (ReqItem1/ReqItemCount1), confirming the tooltip's "Global Token, exchangeable at a
-- vendor" claim and resolving diag-P-token-exchange.md's open question: this is a real
-- token-for-item exchange, not a gold/free catalog. Decoded ids (lowest of 3 redundant rows per
-- slot/tier; all require exactly 1 token, no other cost):
--   T1 Normal   chest=40100 legs=40103 head=40104 shoulder=40105 wrist=40106 waist=40107 hands=40108 feet=40109
--   T1 Heroic   chest=40200 legs=40203 head=40204 shoulder=40205 wrist=40206 waist=40207 hands=40208 feet=40209
--   T1 Mythic   chest=40300 legs=40303 head=40304 shoulder=40305 wrist=40306 waist=40307 hands=40308 feet=40309
--   T1 Ascended chest=30200 legs=30203 head=30204 shoulder=30205 wrist=30206 waist=30207 hands=30208 feet=30209
--   T2 Normal   chest=40400 legs=40403 head=40404 shoulder=40405 wrist=40406 waist=40407 hands=40408 feet=40409
--   T2 Heroic   chest=40500 legs=40503 head=40504 shoulder=40505 wrist=40506 waist=40507 hands=40508 feet=40509
--   T2 Mythic   chest=40600 legs=40603 head=40604 shoulder=40605 wrist=40606 waist=40607 hands=40608 feet=40609
--   T2 Ascended chest=30500 legs=30503 head=30504 shoulder=30505 wrist=30506 waist=30507 hands=30508 feet=30509
-- Slot <-> InventoryType mapping used to pick the token: head=1, shoulder=3, chest=5 (and 20,
-- robe), waist=6, legs=7, feet=8, wrist=9, hands=10.
--
-- Items: every class variant of the nine classic Tier 1 sets (Arcanist 201, Prophecy 202,
-- Felheart 203, Nightslayer 204, Cenarion 205, Giantstalker's 206, Earthfury 207, Lawbringer 208,
-- Might 209, Transcendence 211 -- Prophecy/Transcendence are the Alliance/Horde skins of the same
-- Priest T1 set) and the nine classic Tier 2 (BWL) sets (Netherwind 210, Nemesis 212, Bloodfang
-- 213, Stormrage 214, Dragonstalker's 215, Ten Storms 216, Judgement 217, Wrath 218/220,
-- Faith/Vestments 525), identified by item_template.ItemSet (populated from the client
-- ItemSet.dbc per PR #1498, diag-N-tier-sets.md), class=4 (Armor) only. Each set's "Bloodforged"
-- faction-skin twin (same ItemSet id, same bonus) is included per the user's "faction versions,
-- both vendors list all" instruction; "Sanguine"/"Putrid Core" reskins and any non-armor (class
-- <> 4, e.g. the Ring of Faith trinket) rows are excluded as unrelated catalog noise, not part of
-- these 18 sets. T0.5 and AQ40 Tier 2.5 sets are out of scope per the task and were not touched.
--
-- Per-difficulty clones are picked by item id offset from each piece's lowest (Normal) id --
-- confirmed consistent and reproducible across independently-sampled families (Felheart,
-- Dragonstalker's, Judgement, Nightslayer: entry+0=Normal, entry+300000=Heroic,
-- entry+1300000=Mythic, entry+200000=Ascended; this item offset scheme differs from the
-- +100000/+200000/+300000 convention used for creature difficulty variants). A token of a given
-- tier buys the matching tier's clone (1 token = 1 item, per the user's price rule). Gap: the
-- "Bloodforged" faction-skin twin only has Normal+Heroic clones in this DB for most sets (no
-- Mythic/Ascended item id exists for it) -- only the clones that actually exist are wired; no
-- Mythic/Ascended row was invented for the missing Bloodforged pieces.
--
-- Not included: a handful of items sharing a set's piece name but not fitting any of the four
-- offsets (e.g. several extra "Mantle of Prophecy" ids) -- unrelated catalog collisions, not a
-- real clone of this family.

DELETE FROM `npc_vendor` WHERE `entry` IN (14392, 14394);
DELETE FROM `npc_vendor` WHERE `entry` = 14394;
